| 2026-11-01 | **A `stingy` job CANNOT self-requeue by sbatch - the QOS allows ONE job per user, not "1 running + 1 pending".** `sacctmgr show qos partition-stingy` -> `MaxSubmitJobsPerUser=1, MaxJobsPerUser=1`. Job **719222**'s three successor attempts at 19:35:10 / 19:35:20 / 19:35:40 all returned `sbatch: error: QOSMaxSubmitJobPerUserLimit` + `Job violates accounting/QOS policy`. This is the structural reason the "self-requeue before the wall limit" design could never have worked, independent of the preemption. Replacement pattern, now implemented and validated: **(a)** `scontrol requeue $SLURM_JOB_ID` at the wall budget (same job id -> creates no new submission -> QOS cannot reject it); **(b)** an external low-cost watcher job on the CPU `tiny` partition (job 719234, `miflu_chain_driver.sh`) that resubmits after a preemption, which nothing inside a CANCEL-preempted job can survive. `docs/HPC_RUNBOOK.md` corrected (partition row, QOS row, preemptibility row, new "how to chain" row, gotcha 8 struck through); `AGENTS.md` NOT edited | `sacctmgr show qos partition-stingy`; `miflu_a100_chain.log`; `docs/HPC_RUNBOOK.md` |
