| 2026-11-01 | 🧩 **The MISSING LLM-ENCODER ADAPTER exists — `scripts/llm_encoder_backbone.py` (`FrozenLLMEncoder`).** Before this row no code converted an LLM's frozen representation into the benchmark's array, so none of the `docs/LLM_ARMS.md` roster could enter the comparison (blocker 3 of `SKILL.md` §11). The arm mirrors `innovation/backbones/classic_nn.py::_ChannelIndependent`: `(B,7,104)` → per-channel text prompt (z-space values, **4 dp, comma-separated**, deterministic; deliberately **no channel identity and no horizon** in the prompt, so permuting the 7 channels permutes the 7 output rows and the same context is reusable across L) → frozen causal/instruct LLM (`requires_grad=False`, `eval()` forced even when the runner calls `model.train()`, last hidden layer via `extract_last_hidden_state`, one forward pass, no sampling) → **masked mean-pooled last hidden state** → `(B,7,D)` → **ONE shared `nn.Linear(D,L)`** → `(B,7,L)`. Memory discipline: the encoder runs only under `torch.no_grad()` in **`--encoder-batch-size` chunks**, pooled vectors are cached on **CPU** float32 and `release_encoder_to_cpu()` parks the encoder after its pass, so encoder + a full-dataset activation graph never coexist (the 27B arm is 54.73 GB bf16 on A100, job 718976). Determinism: `torch.manual_seed(seed)` before the head, content-addressed cache keyed by `(model_id, revision, prompt_sha256)` (in-memory + optional `--encoder-cache` file; a foreign model's cache is refused). Provenance for the manifest: model id, **pinned revision sha**, torch/transformers/python versions, encoder params (total **and** trainable), head params, pooling rule, device actually used, cache stats. No training was run and no checkpoint was downloaded | `scripts/llm_encoder_backbone.py`; `docs/LLM_ARMS.md` §7 |
